# YouTube Content Intelligence

Lux provides transport-neutral YouTube content intelligence helpers for scoring
video performance, selecting posting windows, matching trends, generating
metadata suggestions, and producing optimization reports.

## Performance Scoring

```elixir
alias Lux.Integrations.YouTube.ContentIntelligence

video = %{
  id: "video-1",
  title: "Elixir agents for YouTube growth",
  views: 1_000,
  likes: 40,
  comments: 10,
  shares: 5,
  impressions: 5_000,
  clicks: 250,
  duration_seconds: 300,
  average_view_duration_seconds: 120,
  tags: ["elixir", "agents"]
}

ContentIntelligence.performance_score(video)
```

## Recommendations

```elixir
ContentIntelligence.recommendations(video)
```

Recommendations cover low click-through rate, retention, engagement, and sparse
tag coverage.

## Posting Windows

```elixir
ContentIntelligence.posting_windows([
  %{weekday: "Tuesday", hour: 9, engagements: 100},
  %{weekday: "Tuesday", hour: 9, engagements: 200},
  %{weekday: "Friday", hour: 18, engagements: 120}
])
```

## Metadata Optimization

```elixir
ContentIntelligence.optimize_metadata(
  %{
    topic: "Elixir agents for YouTube growth",
    summary: "Build channel analytics with agents.",
    tags: ["Elixir", "YouTube"]
  },
  %{
    trends: [
      %{term: "AI agents", score: 20}
    ]
  }
)
```

## Trend Matching

```elixir
ContentIntelligence.match_trends("YouTube AI agents", [
  %{term: "AI agents", score: 10},
  %{term: "YouTube thumbnail", score: 5}
])
```

## Content Report

```elixir
ContentIntelligence.content_report(video, %{
  trends: [%{term: "AI agents", score: 20}],
  posting_samples: [%{weekday: "Tuesday", hour: 9, engagements: 100}]
})
```

The report can be fed into a workflow that updates metadata, schedules tests,
or sends recommendations to an agent for review.
